### Setup And Start

<!-- Describe the starting state: how the play area and pieces are arranged,
what each player begins with, and how play starts. Refer to the pieces described
below rather than listing them twice. -->
[The game begins with the physical field placed on a flat surface. Each goal is positioned at an opposite end of the field, and the ball is placed in the starting position. Players get ready on their respective sides before the match begins. A timer is started to begin the game.]

### Core Gameplay Loop

<!-- Describe the recurring player choices and actions, the rules that connect
them, and what changes as a result. Game state is the current situation, such as
positions, resources, score, or available choices. -->
[Players use their fingers to control and move the ball around the field. They try to create opportunities to shoot toward the opponent's goal while preventing the other player from scoring. Every successful goal changes the score and gives players another reason to compete.]

### Ending And Outcome

<!-- State when play ends and how the outcome is decided. Include win/lose
conditions where applicable, or another clear beginning/end structure. -->
[The game ends when the timer runs out. The player with the most goals wins. If both players have the same number of goals, the match ends in a tie unless a tiebreaker rule is added later.]

